  "requiredPackages": [],
  "requiresToolGroups": [],
  "optionalToolGroups": ["ui"],
  "toolGroupNotes": "Every mcpTool in this scaffold's hierarchy (manage_scene, manage_gameobject, manage_components, manage_camera, find_gameobjects, batch_execute) is in the bridge's default-on `core` group, so no activation step is needed as written -- the HUD here is legacy uGUI built from manage_gameobject + components_to_add. The bridge reports only `core` as enabled by default, but on the live-verified install (2026-10-21) every non-core tool was callable with no manage_tools call at all, so treat `requiresToolGroups`/`optionalToolGroups` as an ownership map for diagnosis, not as steps to run first. If the developer asks for the HUD to be rebuilt with UI Toolkit (UXML/USS/UIDocument) instead, that uses manage_ui, which is declared in the `ui` group (reported off by default): just call manage_ui, and emit `manage_tools(action: \"activate\", group: \"ui\")` only if manage_ui is reported as not existing, expecting that the MCP client may need a refresh or reconnect before a newly activated tool appears.",
  "createdAt": "2026-03-12T00:00:00Z"
}
